# Line endings: LF in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) checks out CRLF, and the
# fullstore container bind-mounts that clone straight into the CS-Cart docroot —
# so the store runs bytes that CI has never seen. That is not theoretical: while
# diagnosing a label-delivery bug, every deployed file measured larger than its
# repo counterpart by exactly its own line count (travel_core/addon.xml 67718 vs
# 68557 = 839 lines, lang_keys.php 8928 vs 9172 = 244 lines, and the same for
# both providers), which made "does the store match the repo?" unanswerable
# until the cause was identified.
#
# It also keeps `composer package` zips byte-identical wherever they are built.
#
# NOTE for existing clones: this file does not rewrite a working tree that is
# already CRLF. Run once, after merging:
#     git add --renormalize .
# (or re-clone). Until then the container keeps its CRLF copies — harmless, but
# the discrepancy stays.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception: cmd.exe misreads labels and
# long lines in LF-only .cmd/.bat files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.svgz binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
